# CODEOWNERS - SCAM CITY
#
# Conservative by design. The only handle asserted here is the repository owner,
# who is the sole author of the repository's commit history. Every other
# per-path owner is commented out until the release captain confirms the
# GitHub usernames - see docs/REPO-SETUP.md, "Confirm CODEOWNERS handles".
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS: a username in CODEOWNERS that does not exist, or that lacks
# write access, silently breaks "Require review from Code Owners". Reviews can
# then never be satisfied and every PR jams. During a 24-hour sprint that is
# fatal, so we start with one owner we know is real and widen it deliberately.
#
# Path ownership for the five agents is enforced by ops/workplan.json and
# ops/scripts/check-ownership.mjs, which run on every PR. CODEOWNERS controls
# *review routing*; the workplan controls *who may change what*. Keep them
# consistent when you uncomment the lines below.

